      "blockId": "tour:itinerary_text:b04d5d61d358e759",
      "field": "itinerary.text",
      "sourceTextSha256": "47b3f32dae384c0fd18dde66a467f15f0f0cac6ceea79556c6d44c917155e597",
      "text": "After breakfast, spend the day exploring the wines of the Uco Valley. At the foot of the Andes, the region is known for its vineyards and wineries.\n\nVisit three wineries with a guide who specialises in wine. Malbec is the region’s main grape variety. During the visits, you’ll learn how the grapes are grown and harvested, how their ripeness is monitored and how the wine is made. See how the local climate and the valley’s setting at the foot of the Andes influence the vineyards, then taste the wines.\n\nYour guide will explain how to hold the glass, what to look for in the flavour and aroma, and which foods pair well with different wines. Lunch is included at one of the wineries. This is a full-day programme.",
      "provenance": {
        "kind": "ai_translation",
        "model": "GPT-6.1 Sol",
        "runId": "ada-en-translator-mw6kz1rj-kl1fzhzh8j"
      }
    },
